WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.733
Are you single now?

2
00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:05.190
I mean, always.

3
00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:06.600
I think you need to live in a place

4
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.870
where you're perpetually single.

5
00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:09.040
I'm single.
Even when

6
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:09.930
you're with someone,

7
00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:11.771
I think you're single, always.

8
00:00:11.771 --> 00:00:14.590
I'm really good at being alone.

9
00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:15.940
Are you good at being alone?

10
00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:17.310
So good at being alone.

11
00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:18.550
It's my favorite thing.

12
00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:20.230
When I've run, like with a bunch of people,

13
00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:22.150
I'm, oh, I love you guys, but, like,

14
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:24.120
I'm truly myself when I'm just alone,

15
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.160
and I think my album was such a manifestation of just,

16
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.400
like, pure alone time.

17
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.233
I'm an only child.

18
00:00:30.233 --> 00:00:31.520
Do you have siblings?

19
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:32.860
Look at us?

20
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.300
I think being an only child and, you know,

21
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.520
loving that alone time was kind of

22
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.340
one of the reasons that I got so into songwriting,

23
00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.173
it's 'cause, you know,

24
00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:43.210
songwriting is kind of like a friend for you,

25
00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:44.700
and so I think that's like

26
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.640
a really amazing part of creation,

27
00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.420
and I think that also comes from being alone

28
00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.440
and also being bored sometimes, too.

29
00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.703
I think boredom is, like,

30
00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.013
what's the word?

31
00:00:55.013 --> 00:00:56.267
Catalyst for a bunch of creative things.

32
00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:58.170
Can anybody get to boredom

33
00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:03.170
in this ADD-enriched social inundation society?

34
00:01:03.437 --> 00:01:05.600
How do you get to boredom?

35
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.170
Oh, it's very hard.

36
00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:08.693
Yeah.

37
00:01:08.693 --> 00:01:10.880 line:15%
I think I, like, force myself to do it now, too.

38
00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:12.530 line:15%
I definitely force myself

39
00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:14.730 line:15%
to sometimes sit at the piano,

40
00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.360 line:15%
even if I have, like, no ideas,

41
00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:17.960
just to, like, fool around.

42
00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:19.620
And I think there's a really, like,

43
00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.460
cool thing about doing something like that.

44
00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:23.940
Do you ever, like, force your phone off?

45
00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:26.980
Take, like, space from things?

46
00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:27.813
Yes.

47
00:01:27.813 --> 00:01:28.646
What is your process?

48
00:01:28.646 --> 00:01:29.479
I need to.

49
00:01:29.479 --> 00:01:31.640
I very much restrict all of my social media,

50
00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:34.060
because I think it's, A, such a time-suck,

51
00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.320
and B, it can make you, like,

52
00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.600
so sad and depressed sometimes

53
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.360
